%SIXMD 1
# @?DPYVIEW - REPLAY A NATIVE TYPE-340 DISPLAY PROGRAM

## @?OPERANDS

### @?FILE
RAW DAIMOS WORD FILE CONTAINING A NATIVE TYPE-340 DISPLAY PROGRAM.

## DESCRIPTION

DPYVIEW SUBMITS FILE ONCE TO THE PHYSICAL /DEV/DPY0 ENDPOINT. THE KERNEL
RETAINS THAT NATIVE PROGRAM AND REPLAYS IT AT A NOMINAL 30 HZ; DPYVIEW DOES
NOT REWRITE THE FILE FOR EACH REFRESH. WHILE ATTACHED TO A TERMINAL, DPYVIEW
BLOCKS IN THE NORMAL TERMINAL INPUT PATH SO CTRL-C TERMINATES THE FOREGROUND
VIEWER THROUGH THE STANDARD INT EVENT. OTHER INPUT IS IGNORED.
THE INPUT IS A SEQUENCE OF 36-BIT PDP-6 WORDS; EACH WORD CONTAINS TWO NATIVE
18-BIT TYPE-340 DISPLAY INSTRUCTIONS. DPYVIEW DOES NOT INTERPRET, SCALE,
TRANSLATE, OR VALIDATE THE PROGRAM.

THE FIRST INSTRUCTION OF EACH FRAME EXECUTES FROM TYPE-340 RESET STATE, SO THE
PROGRAM SHOULD ESTABLISH ITS OWN MODE, INTENSITY, SCALE, AND BEAM POSITION
BEFORE DRAWING.

DPYVIEW LOADS AT MOST 32256 WORDS. THIS LIMIT FITS WITHIN THE CURRENT DXR BSS
FIELD WHILE LEAVING ROOM FOR THE REST OF THE COMMAND IMAGE. WHILE RAW FRAMES
CONTINUE TO ARRIVE, THE
NORMAL RETAINED TERMINAL REFRESH IS TEMPORARILY SUPPRESSED. WHEN DPYVIEW EXITS
OR IS INTERRUPTED, THE RAW-DISPLAY LEASE EXPIRES AUTOMATICALLY AND ORDINARY
TYPE-340 TERMINAL REFRESH RESUMES.

/DEV/TTYDPY0 IS THE SEPARATE RETAINED TEXT TERMINAL AND IS NOT USED BY
DPYVIEW.

## @?EXIT STATUS

### @?0 - INTERRUPTED AFTER SUCCESSFUL DISPLAY
### @?1 - INVALID INPUT, DEVICE ERROR, OR DISPLAY WRITE FAILURE
